==============================================================================================================
MODEL 3 - HYBRID: FROZEN SigLIP + MEDIAPIPE HAND/BODY LANDMARKS (ISL sentence -> English), output log
==============================================================================================================
checkpoint     : experiments/prediction_improvement_v1/runs/H1_siglip_landmarks/best.pt
sha256         : a9736646acb0336f3e16ace713ef2eb589941511353a1f3779dee888e8c54a74
best epoch     : 65 of 100 (training completed; 6.1 min; peak GPU 1.8 GB)
architecture   : 32 frames, two branches on the same frames:
                 A) SigLIP ViT-B/16 google/siglip-base-patch16-224 (frozen) -> 768-d per frame -> clip-mean normalization
                 B) MediaPipe Holistic 0.10.14 -> 233 values per frame (body-relative pose 14 + visibility 7, each hand:
                    body-relative xy 42 + wrist-relative shape 63, hand-detected flags 2) -> Linear 233->256 + LayerNorm + ReLU
                 joined per frame (768 + 256 = 1024) -> Conv1d(k5)+BatchNorm+ReLU+MaxPool2 (14 steps) -> Linear+LayerNorm+ReLU (1024)
                 -> mBART-cc25 encoder 3 layers + decoder 3 layers, 199-token vocabulary, decoder start en_XX
data           : train signers 1-5 (474 clips) | validation signer 6 (94) | test signer 7 not used for this model alone
training       : stage-1 recipe on cached inputs; 100 epochs, batch 16, AdamW lr new layers 0.0003, mBART 0.0001, warm-up 200, label smoothing 0.1, temporal jitter 0.1,
                 SigLIP: random one of 8 cached augmented views; landmarks: random scale +-10%, shift +-0.1, rotation +-5 deg per clip
role           : one of the three models averaged in the final ensemble E3

